      "textEn": "23\n\nThose who lean towards this illusory concept of life will certainly consider the members of the Yadu dynasty\nequal to Krishna in every way and will worship the future descendants of Krishna just like Krishna. In this way, the continuous existence of the Yadu dynasty on Earth is a very big obstacle in the path of spiritual knowledge.\nAnd on Earth, it will become a burden of the Guru. Therefore, to save the world from the threat of the crime of portraying Vishnu as similar to Vishnu's lineage,\nGod decided to crush the Yadu dynasty. Lord Krishna is always affectionate towards his devotees, but when the descendants of Lord Krishna themselves become his\nenemies or become neutral and they do not love the pure devotees of God or do not befriend their servants, then such so-called family members of God become obstacles in their wishes. In this way, the danger remains that ignorant beings start worshiping such enemies of theirs and\nrespect them as close associates of Krishna.\nFor example, considering Kansa as the maternal uncle of Lord Krishna, and considering him as Krishna's obedient servant, would be a completely flawed conclusion. Only with such a delusion,\nthe opponents of God can be accepted as close associates, and those who harbor animosity towards Krishna can be considered as surrendered, subordinate individuals born in their clan. The purpose of the destruction of the Yaduvansh was to eradicate the false arguments of the Mayavadis, who want to consider every object as the same in every way,\nand they make the unfair argument that the enemies of Krishna devotees can be Krishna's family members.\nIt may be. By actions, by virtuous deeds, and by auspicious ones,\nHaving made the world the destroyer of the impurities of the world. Dwelling in the darkness, in the house of Yadu,\nThe sages, having attained the Pindaraka, were created. 11>. Vishwamitra, Kanva, Durvasa, Bhrigu, and Angira.\nKashyapa, Vamadeva, Atri, Vasistha, Narada and other