रणागत भक्त को कृष्ण के",
      "textEn": "35\n\nIndia was formed. Their other 81 sons became proficient Brahmins in the Shrutis, who promoted the path of Sakam Yagya. These nine Yogendras were able to travel anywhere at will, without any hindrance. These were the direct associates of Lord Madhusudan,\nand they used to wander freely to provide security to the various realms of the universe. The human body can be destroyed at any moment, yet it is an extremely rare achievement. From this,\nit is even rarer to have the company of trusted devotees residing in Vaikuntha, the abode of God, while having this human body. Like this,\nthe company of saints, even if it is for a fraction of a moment, is to provide all the benefits to the soul. Therefore, King Nimi provided appropriate seats to the nine Yoginis, worshiped them, and\nbowed down humbly and asked them about the Bhagavata Dharma. Bhagwat Dharma or\npure devotion to God is the only supreme good fortune for the soul. Pleased with such service, God surrenders to the devotee.\nThey surrender themselves.\nTo answer the king's question, the poet spoke thus from among the nine Yoginis, \"Those means of progress,\nwhose description is given by God himself, and by which even fools attain complete self-realization,\nare called Bhagwat Dharma. This Bhagavat Dharma is about to appear in the form of service to the lotus feet of Achyuta Bhagavan,\nand it eradicates all the fear of the living being. To follow this Bhagwat Dharma,\nIf a person runs even with both eyes closed, then he will not stumble and will not fall either. Whatever a person does with his body, mind, speech, intellect, consciousness, senses, and natural instincts, etc.,\nall of that should be offered to Lord Narayana. Those who do not have love for the lotus feet of God\nbecome subject to Maya (illusion). They forget the form of God and get trapped in the noose of Maya by considering themselves mortal. Coming into the cycle of physical attraction, they become extremely frightened.\nTherefore, the best thing for them is that they offer their lives to a worthy guru,\nand worship the supreme controller of Maya, the Lord, with complete devotion. Just as by eating,\nthe hunger slowly subsides and satisfaction is obtained from every morsel, similarly, to the surrendered devotee, Krishna's"
