      "textEn": "37\n\nThey were very eager to stay close to Lord Krishna and continue to worship him. Because of Daksha's curse,\nNarad is not allowed to live continuously in any place. But Shridhar Swami indicated\nThat there is no effect of curses or other such evils in Dwarka,\nbecause Dwarka is the abode of God and is always protected by his arms, as is evident from the words Govind-Bhuja-\nGuptayam. Bound beings, under the empire of Maya, against the cruel rules of nature,\ncontinue to struggle with birth, death, old age, and disease. But if these bound souls are fortunate enough to enter the abode of God,\nDwarka, Mathura, or Vrindavan, and they live under the direct protection of Lord Krishna's\nall-powerful arms, then they will experience the infinite joy of real life, which is eternal and is the cause of living in the personal association of God. Ko nu rajanindriyavanmukundacharanambujam.\nNot worshiped by all, the best of immortals. 2. Meaning of the word\n\nWho - Who; Nu-indeed; Rajan - O King; Indriya-vant - Endowed with senses; Mukunda-charan-Ambujam - Of Lord Mukunda's\nFeet; Na Bhajet - Will not worship; Sarvatath-Mrityu-h - Facing death from all sides; Upashayam - Worthy of worship; Amar-\nUttamaih - By the best liberated men 1.\n\nO King, in this material world, bound souls face death at every step of life. Therefore, who among the bound souls will not serve the lotus feet of Lord Mukunda, who is even more venerable than the greatest liberated being? Meaning: In this verse, the word 'indriyavan' (endowed with senses) is important. It means \"one with the senses\". Although,\nwe are bound within the physical world, but by the grace of God, we have received a human body, in which\nthere are various senses such as eyes, ears, tongue, nose, and skin.\nGenerally, bound beings use these senses for sensual gratification,\nin a false attempt to exploit the material nature. But,\nour physical senses and their objects are momentary, and being endowed with these momentary objects given by Maya,\nit is not possible to remain calm or happy in the effort to satisfy one's momentary senses. In fact,\nour relentless efforts to satisfy the physical senses inevitably lead to adverse results, that is, physical\nsuffering. The male is attracted to the female. From the awakening of lust, he with her"
